/* NOT a scroll container, and never becomes one. The stack is sized by
   --np-slot-h (built in styles.card): the budget split between the live
   tiles, each taking min(its natural size, its slot). One or two tiles
   are full size and the stack packs tighter as sources arrive, so there
   is nothing to scroll and nothing to clip. A max-height here would only
   ever be the thing that traps a tile half off the bottom, which is
   exactly what this replaced.
   The side padding is the entrance animation's own --np-enter-shift, and
   the negative margin hands that space back to the layout. */
#container{
  overflow: visible;
  padding: var(--np-stack-pad-y, 22px) var(--np-enter-shift, 30px);
  margin: calc(-1 * var(--np-stack-pad-y, 22px)) calc(-1 * var(--np-enter-shift, 30px));
}
